  "title": "The Exact Dimension Threshold for Local Lewis-Weight Acceleration",
  "batch_label": "64",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Let p>2, let A in R^{m x n} have full column rank and strictly positive row-wise ell_p Lewis weights w, put gamma=1-2/p, W=Diag(w), P=W^{gamma/2} A (A^T W^gamma A)^{-1} A^T W^{gamma/2}, and K=W^{-1}(P circ P). Then: (1) for every such A, if m>n(n+1)/2, lambda_min(K)=0 and the predicted local contraction factor is exactly 1-2/p; and (2) for every pair n<=m<=n(n+1)/2 and every p>2 there exists such an A for which K is positive definite.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
